  "text": "},${{r}}\\) in terms of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\nTo find the area of the intersection of the triangle and the semicircle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the radius \\(r\\) of the semicircle.\n2. Determine the area of the triangle.\n3. Determine the area of the semicircle.\n4. Find the area of the intersection of the triangle and the semicircle.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the radius \\(r\\) of the semicircle\n\nThe radius \\(r\\) of the semicircle is the hypotenuse of the right triangle. Using the Pythagorean theorem, we have:\n\\[ r^2 = a^2 + b^2 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine the area of the triangle\n\nThe area \\(A_{\\text{triangle}}\\) of the right triangle with legs \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2}ab \\]\n\n### Step 3: Determine the area of the semicircle\n\nThe area \\(A_{\\text{semicircle}}\\) of the semicircle with radius \\(r\\) is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{semicircle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi r^2 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Find the area of the intersection of the triangle and the semicircle\n\nThe area of the intersection is the area of the triangle minus the area of the segment of the semicircle that is outside the triangle. The area of the segment of the semicircle can be found by subtracting the area of the triangle from the area of the semicircle:\n\\[ A_{\\text{segment}} = A_{\\text{semicircle}} - A_{\\text{triangle}} \\]\n\nSince the triangle is entirely within the semicircle, the area of the intersection is simply the area of the triangle:\n\\[ A_{\\text{intersection}} = A_{\\text{triangle}} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). The roots of the equation \\(x^2 - 12x + 32 = 0\\) are given by the quadratic formula:\n\\[ x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\]\nHere, \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -12\\), and \\(c = 32\\), so:\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 128}}{2} = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} = \\frac{12 \\pm 4}{2} \\]\nThus, the roots are \\(a = 8\\) and \\(b = 4\\).\n\nNow, we can find \\(r\\):\n\\[ r^2 = a^2 + b^2 = 8^2 + 4^2 = 64 + 16 = 80 \\]\n\\[ r = \\sqrt{80} = 4\\sqrt{5} \\]\n\nThe area of the triangle is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2}ab = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8 \\cdot 4 = 16 \\]\n\nThe area of the semicircle is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{semicircle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi r^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (4\\sqrt{5})^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\cdot 80 = 40\\pi \\]\n\nThe area of the intersection is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{intersection}} = A_{\\text{triangle}} = 16 \\]\n\nThus, the area of the intersection of the triangle and the semicircle is:\n\\[ \\boxed{16} \\]",
